<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Device Admin policy for Saatiril — used ONLY for Screen Pinning /
    Lock Task Mode (kiosk mode) during live ceremonies.

    Why this is needed:
    - Android's startLockTask() API has two tiers:
      (a) Non-Device-Owner: shows a system confirmation dialog each time
          ("Pin this app?"), and the user can unpin via a long-press of
          Back+Recents. Good for ad-hoc pinning.
      (b) Device Owner: app is whitelisted via setLockTaskPackages(), so
          startLockTask() works WITHOUT confirmation, AND the user cannot
          exit without the app calling stopLockTask(). True kiosk mode.
    - Tier (b) requires the device to be set as Device Owner via ADB:
          dpm set-device-owner com.saatiril.andro/.admin.SaatirilDeviceAdminReceiver
      (one-time setup; requires no accounts on the device).
    - This DeviceAdminReceiver is the component Android invokes to grant
      Device Owner status. It contains NO policy logic — Saatiril does
      not enforce password/camera/wipe policies. The receiver exists
      purely so dpm has a target to bind to.

    The <uses-policies> block declares the MINIMUM policies needed for
    Device Admin. We keep it empty (no uses-policies tag) because we
    don't actually use any device-admin policies beyond Lock Task Mode,
    which is granted by Device Owner status itself, not by policy XML.
-->
<device-admin xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- Intentionally empty — no password / camera / wipe policies.
         Lock Task Mode whitelisting is a Device Owner capability, not
         a device-admin policy. -->
</device-admin>
